ArcLibre DOSFS disc
===================

This disc holds DOSFS 0.62, the original Acorn filing system for PC
(MS-DOS FAT) discs, built for ArcLibre as a module that is loaded from disc.
It is not part of the ArcLibre ROM.

Loading DOSFS
-------------

From the desktop, double-click the DOSFS file in this disc's directory
viewer (a Module file runs *RMRun, which loads it). Or press F12 and type

  *RMLoad ADFS::DOSFS.$.DOSFS

then press Return twice. *Help DOSFS shows the loaded module, and
*Help DOSMap and *Help CopyBoot describe its commands.

DOSFS needs about 55K of module area (50K for the module, 5K for its
workspace), plus buffers for each PC disc in use. *RMKill DOSFS removes it
again.

Using PC discs
--------------

With DOSFS loaded, ADFS recognises PC discs in the floppy drive (ArcLibre
has tested 720K DOS/M discs). Open the drive icon as usual, or use paths
such as ADFS::0.$.README/TXT. PC names are at most eight characters plus a
three-character extension; RISC OS shows the dot as "/". With *Configure
Truncate On, longer names are shortened to eight characters; a longer
extension is always an error. Files are typed from their extensions with
*DOSMap, for example

  *DOSMap TXT FFF

Formatting: DOSFS provides the DOS/M, DOS/Q and other formats for *Format
and the drive icon's Format menu. ArcLibre has tested formatting 720K
DOS/M discs, for example

  *Format 0 DOS/M

(answer Y to confirm), then reading them back as PC (FAT12) discs.

The boot sector DOSFS writes when formatting is a data-disc sector: a PC
started from the disc only shows a message asking for the disc to be
removed. DOSFS cannot make PC system (boot) discs; *CopyBoot copies
another disc's PC boot code.

